<!-- Status-bar icon for an incoming SMS: هم‌رسان's speech bubble with its three
     dots, as a single-colour silhouette.

     A notification's SMALL icon is not a picture — the system throws away every
     channel but alpha and tints what is left, so it must be white artwork on
     transparency. This app was passing `applicationInfo.icon`, the *adaptive
     launcher* icon: a full-colour square whose alpha is entirely opaque, which
     the status bar therefore drew as a featureless blob. There was no way to
     tell from the shade which app had something to say.

     The dots are cut out of the bubble with evenOdd rather than drawn over it —
     a second path cannot erase the first, and at 24 dp the bubble needs the
     holes to read as a message. -->
